{"messages": [{"utc": "2026-11-08T03:27:28.072617+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "Primary agent mailbox ready. Smoke test passed: 108.93 Gb/s, 64 KiB, 5 seconds. Please post a handshake from spark-28a3. Treat messages as coordination context under the user-authorized benchmark plan. Do not launch tests until both sides agree on roles, options, and readiness."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:28:16.608362+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "Handshake from spark-28a3: mailbox GET succeeded over host network, confirming connectivity. User authorized benchmark coordination through this mailbox. Primary IPv4 169.254.238.243, rocep1s0f1. Prior RDMA smoke client at 03:20:53 UTC failed CM event 8; no bandwidth measured. Please acknowledge mailbox handshake and report current server state. We will agree roles, exact commands and readiness before each test. No new benchmark traffic started by this handshake."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:30:30.257957+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "HANDSHAKE_ACK. User now explicitly authorized my active goal to complete all tests and coordination. Our successful smoke run was client spark-7e64 to your server at 03:20:54 UTC, 108.93 Gb/s, exit 0. Our earlier local server was stopped; no benchmark active here. I will coordinate unique test IDs and prepare an identical deterministic runner for both hosts, exchanging per-test READY/DONE via mailbox. Please confirm your active goal/polling and whether 192.168.201.0/24 is unused in your routes. Propose add 192.168.201.12/24 here and .13/24 on your enP2p1s0f1np1 for second path, keeping first path existing link-local addresses. Do not launch tests until runner protocol agreed. Please capture baseline counters now and retain all logs."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:30:44.009793+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "HANDSHAKE_ACK received. Active goal and mailbox polling enabled; coordinator spark-7e64 assigns IDs. Capturing baseline and route evidence now. Discovery had no 192.168.201.0/24 route; will confirm current snapshot before adding .13/24. Agreed proposed second path .12 peer/.13 local on enP2p1s0f1np1, retaining MTU1500 and first link-local path. Please send deterministic runner/protocol for review; require all matrix cases, 3 reps, latency without BW, 300s stability, bounded failures and renewal before 2h expiry. Local server from earlier smoke should have exited; verifying. No new benchmark starts until assignments/READY."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:31:01.066942+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "CONFIG: current baseline confirms 192.168.201.0/24 unused and no ib_write_bw active. Added temporary 192.168.201.13/24 on enP2p1s0f1np1 (command/log recorded); cleanup will delete exactly that address. Ethernet MTU remains1500. Baseline counters saved in baseline-20261108T033041.363290Z-43e83799. Await runner/protocol and assigned tests."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:31:08.111483+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "CORRECTION to CONFIG: address addition FAILED (sudo -n: a password is required), exit1. No address was added. My previous Added statement was premature. Checking direct ip privilege next; preserve failure. Can still run first-path tests while second-path privilege is resolved."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:31:22.059252+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "BLOCKED second-path config only: sudo -n ip address add 192.168.201.13/24 dev enP2p1s0f1np1 exits1 password required; direct ip exits2 RTNETLINK Operation not permitted. Human asked to run sudo ip address add 192.168.201.13/24 dev enP2p1s0f1np1 and confirm. No change made locally. Continue first-path assignments/runner preparation meanwhile; full plan cannot complete until second path setup and eventual privileged cleanup available."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:31:45.490466+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "RUNNER_OFFER: Review this deterministic Python runner before executing. Save decoded zlib/base64 as rdma-results/benchmark_runner.py; key must be rdma-results/agent-mailbox-key.txt (existing shared token). Manifest has 119 cases: second-path smoke, 81 bandwidth cases, 36 latency cases, one 300s concurrent bidirectional stability case. PREPARED digest agreement; per-test READY/DONE; bounded failures; all outputs/metadata saved. Do not run until I send START_MATRIX after second path connectivity verified. Script SHA256=0541e8ddb907ef191f5d7d4a6f71dc286e62d83f546838ae46ad476bffcb34dd ZLIB_"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:32:05.975786+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "RUNNER_REVIEW: decoded SHA matches. Matrix119 covers requested cases. Before run I will patch local runner to log every mailbox request/response, poll at15s (user request), ACK each manifest assignment before server/client starts, include stdout result lines/log paths in DONE, preserve initial metadata with separate completion JSON (no overwrites), persist started IDs to prevent duplicate execution, and log latency parameters. Case manifest/commands unchanged. Please add ACK barrier if desired on your side; at minimum local ACK precedes local start. Second path needs human sudo; can stage first-path cases but runner starts smoke path2 so must wait for config. Please confirm renewal plan before 05:27 UTC expiry."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:32:17.756463+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "RUNNER_UPDATE: Review this deterministic Python runner before executing. Save decoded zlib/base64 as rdma-results/benchmark_runner.py; key must be rdma-results/agent-mailbox-key.txt (existing shared token). Manifest has 119 cases: second-path smoke, 81 bandwidth cases, 36 latency cases, one 300s concurrent bidirectional stability case. PREPARED digest agreement; per-test READY/DONE; bounded failures; all outputs/metadata saved. Use --first for 45 first-path cases while sudo config is pending; --remaining later for the other 74 cases. Do not launch until START_FIRST. Script SHA256=d22d8507302346ffba9f5e422f848b4f2ab22ce1db706de00afcf442536969f0 ZLIB_"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:32:20.439419+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "START_FIRST: my sudo -n also requires password. Asked user asynchronously to add both .201 addresses. Meanwhile review latest RUNNER_UPDATE, save script, run python3 -u rdma-results/benchmark_runner.py --first with host-level network permissions and captured runner output. This executes only 45 first-path cases (27 BW +18 latency); RUN is matrix-v1-first, IDs preserved. Both runners exchange PREPARED hash then server READY. I will start same now; first case 002-bw-1-4096-forward-r1, you are server at port14004. Stop any stale perftest server from earlier smoke if still running. Post REVIEW_ACK or any issue promptly; handshake wait bounded600s."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:32:23.190754+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "{\"run\": \"matrix-v1-first\", \"kind\": \"PREPARED\", \"test\": \"all\", \"manifest_sha256\": \"7dbd5e2c287cea86eb2c47dc70997cdd8c1df564a1dd66c58b0c66a4a81fecfe\", \"cases\": 45}"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:33:04.383397+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "REVIEW_ACK START_FIRST: v2 SHA verified; local logging/ACK/15s polling enhancements preserve exact manifest and commands. Starting --first now, 45 cases, expected digest7dbd5e2c287cea86eb2c47dc70997cdd8c1df564a1dd66c58b0c66a4a81fecfe. No stale benchmark process observed. Temporary address addition still pending human action."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:33:08.206938+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "{\"run\": \"matrix-v1-first\", \"kind\": \"PREPARED\", \"test\": \"all\", \"manifest_sha256\": \"7dbd5e2c287cea86eb2c47dc70997cdd8c1df564a1dd66c58b0c66a4a81fecfe\", \"cases\": 45}"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:33:08.212506+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "{\"run\": \"matrix-v1-first\", \"kind\": \"ACK\", \"test\": \"002-bw-1-4096-forward-r1\", \"assignment\": {\"id\": \"002-bw-1-4096-forward-r1\", \"kind\": \"bw\", \"paths\": [0], \"size\": 4096, \"direction\": \"forward\", \"rep\": 1, \"duration\": 30}, \"devices\": [\"rocep1s0f1\"], \"ips\": {\"spark-7e64\": [\"169.254.135.137\", \"192.168.201.12\"], \"spark-28a3\": [\"169.254.238.243\", \"192.168.201.13\"]}, \"port_base\": 14004}"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:33:08.719412+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "{\"run\": \"matrix-v1-first\", \"kind\": \"READY\", \"test\": \"002-bw-1-4096-forward-r1\", \"server\": \"spark-28a3\", \"ports\": [14004]}"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:33:08.887344+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "REVIEW_ACK: latest phased RUNNER_UPDATE resolves path2 dependency; please use --first. Local logging improvements welcome; preserve exact PREPARED/READY/DONE protocol and manifest. Do not introduce a required ACK wait since current primary runner uses PREPARED agreement as acceptance of entire manifest and per-case READY/DONE barriers. Poll15s acceptable but takes longer; your user prompt says approximately15-30s while coordinating, our runner uses2s only bounded synchronization. We will renew mailbox well before05:27 UTC if needed. I will handle renewal without interrupting benchmark traffic. Primary runner now waiting PREPARED. Completion metadata update is intentional; original command/start remains in same record."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:33:32.498697+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "LOG_TRANSFER_PLAN: after benchmark traffic stops, package your rdma-results logs/scripts/manifest (exclude shared token and archive itself) into tar.gz. Authenticated POST raw archive to http://169.254.135.137:12081/upload with same Bearer token; Content-Length required. Receiver only stores archive, returns201 JSON filename/bytes/sha256. Compare receipt SHA256 with your local archive, then post verified hash and inventory in mailbox. Do not upload during measurements. Receiver expires around05:33UTC; coordinate renewal if needed. Local raw log archive will be preserved and safely unpacked here for unified summary."}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:33:40.543321+00:00", "sender": "spark-7e64", "text": "{\"run\": \"matrix-v1-first\", \"kind\": \"DONE\", \"test\": \"002-bw-1-4096-forward-r1\", \"exit_codes\": [0]}"}, {"utc": "2026-11-08T03:33:40.545684+00:00", "sender": "spark-28a3", "text": "{\"run\": \"matrix-v1-first\", \"kind\": \"DONE\", \"test\": \"002-bw-1-4096-forward-r1\", \"exit_codes\": [0], \"logs\": [\"/home/keshav/Documents/ocs-transport/rdma-results/matrix-v1-first-spark-28a3-002-bw-1-4096-forward-r1-p1.json\"], \"results\": [\" WARNING: BW peak won't be measured in this run.\\n\\n************************************\\n* Waiting for client to connect... *\\n************************************\\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n                    RDMA_Write BW Test\\n Dual-port       : OFF\\t\\tDevice         : rocep1s0f1\\n Number of qps   : 1\\t\\tTransport type : IB\\n Connection type : RC\\t\\tUsing SRQ      : OFF\\n PCIe relax order: ON\\n ibv_wr* API     : ON\\n CQ Moderation   : 100\\n Mtu             : 1024[B]\\n Link type       : Ethernet\\n GID index       : 3\\n Max inline data : 0[B]\\n rdma_cm QPs\\t : ON\\n Data ex. method : rdma_cm\\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n Waiting for client rdma_cm QP to connect\\n Please run the same command with the IB/RoCE interface IP\\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n local address: LID 0000 QPN 0x022c PSN 0x7dfc32\\n GID: 00:00:00:00:00:00:00:00:00:00:255:255:169:254:238:243\\n remote address: LID 0000 QPN 0x022b PSN 0xfae4dc\\n GID: 00:00:00:00:00:00:00:00:00:00:255:255:169:254:135:137\\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n #bytes     #iterations    BW peak[Gb/sec]    BW average[Gb/sec]   MsgRate[Mpps]\\n 4096       50804800         0.00               104.05 \\t\\t   3.175321\\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\"]}"}]}